      "note": "1073DPA and 1073DPD User Guide issue 3, opened 2026-11-12 (read as text): rear panel mic in 1 and 2 (XLR), line in 1 and 2 (XLR/TRS combos, modelled as their XLR half), line out 1 and 2 (XLR), ADC in 1 and 2 (TRS inserts, not modelled), AES out 1 and 2 (XLR), AES sync in, word clock in and out (BNC), DSD out (BNC, no signal type), IEC mains connector (type letter not named: iec-c14 assumed, plan assumedConnectors power-in); front panel gain, trim, 48 V and input selector; a mains switch exists but its panel is not stated (drawn on the front). The DPD has no EQ. Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, knobs and indicators drawn at the port positions, no photo, no logo, no lettering. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess): no drawing or photo was opened. Connector genders not stated by the source follow the convention input = female, output = male."
